{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and a prince of the Crusader state of the County of Tripoli. He was born in around 1140 and died in 1187. Raymond was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. *## Early Life* Raymond's early life was marked by the assassination of his father in 1152 when he was around 12 years old. His mother Hodierna took charge as regent until he came of age. After his father's death Raymond was taken to the court of his uncle King Baldwin III of Jerusalem where he was raised.\n\n*### Regency in Jerusalem* Raymond's involvement in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem began early. In 1174 King Amalric I of Jerusalem died and Raymond became regent for the young King Baldwin IV. As regent Raymond was responsible for arranging the marriage of the King's sister Sibylla to William Longsword of Montferrat. However this marriage was short-lived as William died in 1177. Raymond's regency ended when Baldwin IV came of age.\n\nRaymond's relationship with the King was strained due to his opposition to the King's marriage to Guy of Lusignan. Raymond was a member of the faction that opposed Guy's rise to power and was a supporter of Raymond of Antioch. *#### The Battle of Hattin* The tension between Raymond and Guy came to a head in 1187 when the Kingdom of Jerusalem was invaded by Saladin. Raymond was forced to make an alliance with Saladin to protect his own county. This alliance was seen as treasonous by the other Crusader leaders and Raymond was blamed for the defeat at the Battle of Hattin. The battle was a disastrous loss for the Crusaders and marked a turning point in the history of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. Raymond died soon after the battle. His death marked the end of an era for the County of Tripoli and the Crusader states. Raymond's legacy was complex and multifaceted and his actions continue to be debated by historians today. He had no children and the County of Tripoli passed to his godson Raymond IV.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.018178174272179604}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.5497195136049413e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0005538121913559735}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0016018429305404425}, {"token": " nob", "logprob": -0.15810136497020721}, {"token": "leman", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.032599885016679764}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.4980226755142212}, {"token": " prince", "logprob": -1.0492748022079468}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0310127642005682}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -0.007616054266691208}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " state", "logprob": -0.31331175565719604}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0008905735448934138}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.6933193206787109}, {"token": " County", "logprob": -1.7881377516459906e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.005448491778224707}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.0026806395035237074}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.000504723924677819}, {"token": " born", "logprob": -0.1106729730963707}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.6932007074356079}, {"token": " around", "logprob": -1.1373867988586426}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "114", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.00033968876232393086}, {"token": " died", "logprob": -0.10201002657413483}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.00026127262390218675}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0004447901446837932}, {"token": "118